    <statement><tabular xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" valign="top">
<row>
<cell>Suppose the region on the left in the figure 
(with blue shading) has area is 15, and the
region on the right (with green shading) has 
area 5.  Using the graph of <m>f(x)</m> in
the figure, find the following integrals.
<m>\displaystyle \int_a^b f(x) \, dx =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0001"/>
<m>\displaystyle \int_b^c f(x) \, dx =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0002"/>
<m>\displaystyle \int_a^c f(x) \, dx =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0003"/>
<m>\displaystyle \int_a^c |f(x)| dx =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0004"/></cell>
<cell>
<image pi:generated="webwork/images/def-int-areas-5-image-1.png" width="50%"/>
<p>Graph of <m>y = f(x)</m></p></cell>
</row>
</tabular>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-15</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-10</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>20</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>y = f(x)</m> and the <m>x</m>-axis, with area below the axis being
counted as negative area.  Therefore



<m>\int_a^b f(x) dx = -15</m>,
<m>\int_b^c f(x) dx = 5</m>,
<m>\int_a^c f(x) dx = -15 + 5 = -10</m>, and
<m>\int_a^c |f(x)| dx = |-15| + |5| = 20</m>.



</solution>
